      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Maxillary sinusitis can cause pain or discomfort to the maxillary dentition but no report of patients complaining of a \"jumping tooth sensation\" during sinusitis has been recorded in the literature. This article presents a case of an unusual localised sensation from a maxillary right second premolar experienced while undergoing root canal treatment. This sensation was felt during walking while the patient was suffering an episode of influenza. This sensation first occurred following debridement of the root canal. However, it persisted even after the root canal had been sealed. A hypothetical explanation of this manifestation is proposed."},
